       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the maximum daily dose for adults in a monitored setting (3,200 mg/day). The 1600 mg single dose is also double the usual maximum of 800 mg per dose. This level carries a serious risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum for inflammatory conditions\n- **400\u2013600 mg PO every 6 hours** (1,600\u20132,400 mg/day), the usual range for pain or fever\n- **1600 mg total per day**, divided (for example, 400 mg four times daily)\n\nIf you do want 1600 mg four times daily, tell me and give me the clinical rationale. I can enter it with a note on the order, though pharmacy may still contact you to verify it.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it."
